This setter is almost certainly not on the decode path, so no rewrite of it will measurably change decode time. The version below makes the call explicit through `this->` and a named constant. It produces the same call with the same arguments, so behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
    void SetMaxNegVerticalSpeed(FIT_FLOAT32 maxNegVerticalSpeed)
    {
        static constexpr FIT_UINT8 kFieldNum = 48;
        this->SetFieldFLOAT32Value(kFieldNum, maxNegVerticalSpeed, 0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```